During my semester break in September 2024, my team, Zenith Technologies, took part in the SP Batey Hackathon at Singapore Polytechnic. We went in with one problem in mind: many families throw away food simply because they forgot they had it.

## Designing Frésko

We designed Frésko in Figma, an app that tracks the expiry dates of your food, scans grocery receipts to add the items for you, sends reminders before the food goes bad and suggests recipes to use it up.

This idea secured us a place in the grand finals of the hackathon!

## The Idea Stayed With Me

After the hackathon, the design stayed in Figma while I completed my diploma, interned at Amber Creative and took on freelance projects. However, the idea kept coming back to me.

In April 2026, I decided to start building it for real on my own, and I named it StillGood.

## Going Live

On 26 August 2026, StillGood went live on the Google Play Store. The core idea is still the same as our hackathon design: know what is in your kitchen and use it before it expires. It has been quite a journey, and I am grateful to my team for where it all started.
